{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_6d4vglbie72fc6gxu7snlfdewlu5np625jq3e4e7hzd3xqu3snhq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete — all four phases pass. Summary:\n\n## What the library is\n`c_src/` is a single translation unit exporting exactly one symbol:\n```c\nvoid normalize(float *dest, const float *src, int size);\n```\n`Cargo.toml` declares no optional features (`default = []`) and `CMakeLists.txt` no options/`#ifdef`s → **exactly one feature combination** (`--no-default-features`), verified in both `dev` and `release`.\n\n## Artifacts created (crate root)\n| file | content |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` | `nm -D` inventory; C exports `normalize`, Rust exports `normalize`; **symbol diff empty**, 0 undefined non-libc symbols |\n| `ERRORS.md` | 24-row error-surface table mechanically derived from the only 4 branches in the C (`i<size`, `sum>0.0f`, `dest!=src`) + every UB input a C caller can pass; all 24 rows `[x]` |\n| `CONFIGS.md` | 98-row configuration table: 6 aliasing modes × 14 value classes × 25 sizes × overlap distances, plus alignment sweep, composed pipelines, overflow/underflow edges, permutations, full-domain sweep, fuzz; all 98 rows `[x]` |\n| `tests/` | 6 files, 50 tests, ~2200 lines — both `.so`s loaded via `libloading`, **never** calling Rust directly |\n| `scripts/verify_all.sh` | enumerates the feature powerset from `Cargo.toml`, runs check/build/test for each × `dev`/`release`, then diffs `nm -D` |\n\nRoughly **800 000 paired C↔Rust FFI invocations**, compared bit-for-bit over the *whole* backing allocation (guard elements + `src` buffer included, so stray/missing writes are caught).\n\n## Divergences found and fixed\n1. **Real behavioural divergence (UB paths).** For `src`/`dest == NULL` with `size > 0`, the C `.so` dies with **SIGSEGV (11)** but the Rust `.so` died with **SIGABRT (6)**: rustc's debug-assertion `CheckNull` pass injects `null pointer dereference occurred` → non-unwinding panic → `abort()`. gcc emits no such check. Fixed by disabling those runtime checks for this crate (`[profile.dev] debug-assertions/overflow-checks = false`, documented in `Cargo.toml` + `ERRORS.md`) and guarded by `err_00_so_is_built_without_ub_runtime_checks`. Both now die with signal 11 on all 5 fatal rows.\n2. `src/lib.rs`: `i += 1` → `i.wrapping_add(1)` so `size == INT_MAX` wraps like gcc's `i++` instead of trapping.\n3. Two harness bugs of my own (undersized buffers in rows 88/89).\n\nThe fatal-signal rows (`ERRORS.md` 5, 6, 11, 12, 24) are compared in **child processes** using a page-aligned region with a `PROT_NONE` guard, so the fault is deterministic and the two children's `(signal, code)` must be *equal* — not merely \"both failed\".\n\n## Anti-vacuity checks\n`tests/meta.rs` proves the suite isn't green-by-accident: an intentionally perturbed implementation (`x/sqrt(sum)` instead of `x*(1/sqrt(sum))`, NaN propagation instead of zero-fill) is **rejected** by the same comparison (694 catches), and the generators demonstrably reach all three C branches (`sum>0`: 2009, `memset`: 397, `dest==src` no-op: 394, `sum==+inf`: 1100, `sum==NaN`: 233, underflowed `sum`: 62).\n\nAdditionally, the entire suite also passes against a C `.so` rebuilt with `-O3`, so the match doesn't depend on the C optimisation level. `c_src/` sources are untouched (only the requested `build/` directory was added)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1471,"cache_read_input_tokens":132314,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1471,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"143ab64a-bf2a-43d7-bf0d-0f01bd7fc8e6","uuid":"3816a0ef-fdfe-488c-b535-fe9bac0d42aa","timestamp":"2026-08-19T14:19:37.506Z"}
